        },
        {
          "text": "Here are some important facts about twist knots.",
          "bbox": [
            130.32,
            551.57,
            323.49,
            564.86
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "Times-Roman"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            9.96
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "(1) By deﬁnition, if n ∈{0, 1} then J(2, n) and J(−2, −n) are the unknot. Also observe",
          "bbox": [
            135.24,
            566.45,
            477.22,
            586.34
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "Times-Italic",
            "Times-Roman",
            "rtxmi",
            "txsy"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            9.96
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "that J(2, −1) and J(−2, 1) are isotopic to J(−2, −2) and J(2, 2) respectively (for",
          "bbox": [
            151.8,
            578.33,
            477.08,
            598.22
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "Times-Italic",
            "Times-Roman",
            "rtxmi",
            "txsy"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            9.96
          ]
        },
        {
